//! error/types — Error type definitions.
//!
//! Status: reserved (M3 foundation, stdlib/SPEC.md §4).
//!
//! M3 error convention (SPEC.md §4, "Error conventions"):
//! - E1: `panic(msg)` for violated preconditions / invariant failures.
//! - E2: `Option<T>` for absence-is-not-error.
//! - E3: `Result<T, String>` for foundation fallible fns that must explain failure.
//! - E4: `?` / `??` are the only propagation tools; no exceptions.
//!
//! There is no `Error` trait in M3 and `E` in `Result<T, E>` stays an
//! ordinary type — `String` is the error type throughout M3 (E3). Typed
//! error enums (enums carrying structured error payloads) land with M4,
//! when the trait/impl system (SPEC.md C4) is in place.
//!
//! Unblock condition: M4 trait + enum-with-payload support.
